WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.750
Well, Brighter Tomorrow Therapy is all about compassionate, accessible mental health care.

2
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:10.050
I have owner Yvette Howard joining me now, so let's start with your journey from medical

3
00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:12.150
social worker to now.

4
00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:17.770
How has that really shaped your idea of the care that you're hoping to provide to our

5
00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.770
city?

6
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:21.770
Yes, and thank you for having me.

7
00:00:21.770 --> 00:00:30.090
I was a medical social worker for the hospitals, local hospitals here, hospice and

8
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:37.970
dialysis, but the main focus that got me to Brighter Tomorrow was working in dialysis.

9
00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:43.250
When I worked there, I would provide resources to patients.

10
00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:51.490
When I hand off the referral source for therapy, a lot of the patients declined.

11
00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:58.170
When I saw that, I noticed there was a need for a therapist who could support patients

12
00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:03.490
who were struggling with chronic pain, chronic illness, some kind of medical condition, so

13
00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:07.930
they can feel heard, seen, and I wanted to be that advocate for them.

14
00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:13.450
They felt unheard, they felt like the therapist wouldn't understand them, especially when

15
00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:16.890
going to dialysis three days a week.

16
00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:24.570
It was my calling to be able to support the clients or the patients who were struggling

17
00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:25.570
in that area.

18
00:01:25.570 --> 00:01:30.610
I think there's a lot of stigma around mental health that it's just anxiety and depression,

19
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:35.690
but there's so much more to all of that, so how are you bringing awareness to that?

20
00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:38.050
We use a lot of social media.

21
00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:45.610
We have our Instagram and Facebook pages that we provide educational information on.

22
00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:53.330
We use our blogs, and I also am in the community, so when there's an event going on, I try

23
00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:57.530
to be a vendor at those events.

24
00:01:57.530 --> 00:02:00.250
I also remember just being around.

25
00:02:00.250 --> 00:02:06.810
I was going to get something to eat, and I saw a young lady who just looked very sad

26
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:07.810
at the moment.

27
00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:12.290
I didn't know exactly what she was going through, but I just told her it was okay to get some

28
00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:13.290
help.

29
00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.370
I handed her my business card, and then a few weeks later, she emailed me and was just

30
00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:22.490
thanking me for opening that door to getting help, so just letting people know that it's

31
00:02:22.490 --> 00:02:28.810
okay to not be okay and to recognize what's coming up for you.

32
00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:31.690
Not just in our brain, but in our body.

33
00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:37.570
Sometimes we feel that gut feeling in our stomach, and it's like something's not right.

34
00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:43.570
It's okay to reach out, and to do that, you can go so much online now that you can go

35
00:02:43.570 --> 00:02:46.210
on and find mental health support.

36
00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:48.570
And now, there's so many ways to get in contact with you.

37
00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.570
You have two locations.

38
00:02:49.570 --> 00:02:51.330
Like you said, you have all your social media.

39
00:02:51.330 --> 00:02:53.730
What's the best way for someone to reach out?

40
00:02:53.730 --> 00:03:00.890
You can always call us, is the best way, at 725-238-6990.

41
00:03:00.890 --> 00:03:02.850
You can go on our website as well.

42
00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.810
All of our information is on there.

43
00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:11.090
We have about 17 clinicians who specialize in different modalities and support where

44
00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:16.850
we can help children, middle-aged class, elderly adults, all of it.

45
00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.930
You do these quarterly classes as well.

46
00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.890
It's all there on the website.

47
00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:25.730
Yvette, thank you so much for coming in and sharing all of this with our viewers. brightertomorrowtherapy.com
